// Copyright (c) 2026 Roshan. All rights reserved.// Proprietary license — see LICENSE file for details.package com.roshan.persona.agent.ladb/** * NOUS — LADB Connection State Machine (Module 9 v2 — audit P1). * * Strategy §9 specifies the state machine: *   DISCONNECTED → PAIRING → CONNECTED → AUTHENTICATED → READY * * - **DISCONNECTED** — no connection, no pairing in progress. * - **PAIRING** — SPAKE2+ handshake in progress (wireless debugging pairing). * - **CONNECTED** — TCP socket established, awaiting ADB auth. * - **AUTHENTICATED** — ADB auth handshake complete, can send commands. * - **READY** — fully operational, can execute automation operations. * * Transitions are driven by [LadbConnection] events. Illegal transitions * throw [IllegalStateException] (defensive — bugs in state machine logic). */enum class LadbConnectionState {    DISCONNECTED,    PAIRING,    CONNECTED,    AUTHENTICATED,    READY,}/** * Reason for a transition to DISCONNECTED. * * Used for diagnostics + retry logic. */enum class LadbDisconnectReason {    /** User explicitly disconnected. */    USER_INITIATED,    /** Socket closed by remote (adb daemon stopped). */    REMOTE_CLOSED,    /** Heartbeat timeout — no response in 30s. */    HEARTBEAT_TIMEOUT,    /** Auth failed — wrong key. */    AUTH_FAILED,    /** Network error — WiFi disabled, port closed, etc. */    NETWORK_ERROR,    /** Connection dropped mid-operation — fall back to Accessibility. */    MID_OPERATION_DROP,}